    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5065A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to including community\ncenters with a religious affiliation in the definition of public place\nfor purposes of offenses against public order and including falsely\nreporting an incident and placing a false bomb or hazardous substance\nin the definition of specified offense for the purpose of hate crimes\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nIncludes community centers with a religious affiliation in the\ndefinition of public place for purposes of offenses against public\norder\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Subdivision 1 of section 240.00 of the penal law is amended\nto read as follows:\n\n1. \"Public place\" means a place to which the public or a substantial\ngroup of persons has access, and includes, but is not limited to,\nhighways, transportation facilities, schools, places of amusement,\nparks, playgrounds, community centers with a religious affiliation,\nand hallways, lobbies and other portions of apartment houses and\nhotels not constituting rooms or apartments designed for actual\nresidence.\n\n§ 2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nCurrently section 240.00 of the penal law does not include calling in\nbomb threats to community centers with religious affiliation.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nBomb threats forced evacuations at Jewish schools and community\ncenters in at least 11 states by February 27, 2017 of this year. The\nJewish Community Center Association confirmed threats in states\nranging from Florida to Michigan, as well as Tarrytown and New\nRochelle in Westchester County.\n\nNobody should have to live in fear of his or her lives for any reason\nand especially because of religious beliefs. This legislation expands\nsection 240.00 of the penal law to include any community center with a\nreligious association or affiliation in New York State that receives a\nbomb threat. These threats would be covered by Article 485 of the\nPenal law, which establishes \"Hate Crimes\". Hence, it helps to protect\na person's religious beliefs by going after those people that would\nthreaten our way of life in New York and our country.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
